drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c:821:2-13: ERROR: probable double put.

 Device node iterators put the previous value of the index variable, so an
 explicit put causes a double put.

Generated by: scripts/coccinelle/iterators/device_node_continue.cocci

Fixes: 9f4235d19a73 ("PCI: apple: Probe all GPIOs for availability first")
Reported-by: kernel test robot <lkp@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: kernel test robot <lkp@intel.com>
---

tree:   https://github.com/AsahiLinux/linux smc/work
head:   60ce5f01c74024d326c4ae6880e1f922f6d1712d
commit: 9f4235d19a7390b792c6d00c7541bcefde7c73a7 [14/16] PCI: apple: Probe =
all GPIOs for availability first
:::::: branch date: 4 hours ago
:::::: commit date: 4 hours ago

Please take the patch only if it's a positive warning. Thanks!

 pcie-apple.c |    1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -818,7 +818,6 @@ static int apple_pcie_probe(struct platf
 	/* Check for probe dependencies for all ports first */
 	for_each_child_of_node(dev->of_node, of_port) {
 		ret =3D apple_pcie_probe_port(of_port);
-		of_node_put(of_port);
 		if (ret)
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Port %pOF probe fail\n", of_port);
 	}
